Privacy Policy

DJ Boi Discord Music Bot (“the Bot”) respects your privacy and aims to keep your information safe. This policy explains what data is collected and how it is used.

1. Data Collection

- The Bot does not intentionally collect or store personal information such as usernames, email addresses, or message contents.
- The Bot may temporarily process Discord user IDs, channel IDs, and server (guild) IDs in memory for the purpose of providing its features (such as music playback and queue management).

2. Data Usage

- Data processed by the Bot is used solely to provide music playback and related features as requested by users via Discord commands.

3. Data Storage

- The Bot does not store any data persistently outside of temporary memory necessary for operation.
- No user data is shared with third parties.

4. Third-Party Services

- The Bot uses external services (such as YouTube via yt-dlp and Discord APIs) to provide music streaming functionality. Use of these services is subject to their own privacy policies.

5. Children's Privacy

- The Bot does not knowingly collect or store data from users under the age of 13. If you believe such data has been collected, please contact the maintainer for removal.

6. Changes to this Policy

- This Privacy Policy may be updated from time to time. Continued use of the Bot constitutes acceptance of the current policy.

7. Contact

- For questions or concerns regarding this Privacy Policy, please open an issue on the GitHub repository.

